    "description": "<p>We give a nonvacuous two-dimensional counterexample to the manifold conjecture printed by Krener in OWR11/2009. A smooth observed system on a connected closed genus-three surface has zero dynamics and output in R17 obtained by composing a connected two-sheeted hyperbolic covering with a smooth Nash isometric embedding. Its exact finite-time differential observation Gramian is P_T=T*pi^*g. For every fixed positive T it is geodesically complete with actual sectional curvature -1/T and uniform positive upper and lower bounds relative to any fixed smooth background metric and a fixed finite normalized atlas. The history map is locally injective but every attained history has exactly two initial states.</p><p>The construction is an application of classical constructions, with Nash, covering classification, hyperbolic geometry and older local/global observability ambiguity explicitly credited. A bounded primary-source audit, including complete readings of Dirr2009 and Kang2013 and a fresh independent adversarial priority assessment, found no verified earlier explicit complete construction in inspected sources. Those two named access gaps are closed; older uninspected originals and corpus limits are documented. No absolute firstness, continuous seventeen-year openness, new covering/Nash mechanism, or first refutation of every literal dimensional reading is claimed. A strengthened question restricted to one global Euclidean state domain is outside this result.</p><p>AI tools were used extensively in solving, drafting, reproducing and adversarially reviewing the work. This is an unrefereed preprint without conventional human peer review. The package provides the analytical proof and a dependency-free supplementary exact verifier with recorded results, source and priority supplement, reproducibility instructions, license and file digests. Finite controls do not construct a Nash embedding or machine-certify global topology or completeness.</p>"
  },
